{"id":79,"date":"2011-10-01T20:28:05","date_gmt":"2011-10-01T20:28:05","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.wordpress.com\/?p=79"},"modified":"2021-01-06T12:21:40","modified_gmt":"2021-01-06T12:21:40","slug":"equipment-standard-microphones-setup","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/10\/01\/equipment-standard-microphones-setup\/","title":{"rendered":"Equipment standard (microphones &#8211; setup)"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>My main concern when it comes to microphones is that I want to feel they express the energy of my musical intentions.<\/p>\n<p>Until now, I\u2019ve let sound engineers use their own microphones and I\u2019ve used a split, a return bus or my own built-in microphones to get sound into my setup. So, as <a title=\"Signal-flow\" href=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/13\/signal-flow\/\">previously mentioned<\/a>, it\u2019s up to the engineer to decide the mix between the acoustic drum set and the sounds coming from my computer.<\/p>\n<p>I have a dream &#8230; My own sound engineer.<\/p>\n<p>Well, until then, I\u2019ll have to come up with something else.<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>This is what I\u2019ve been thinking:<\/p>\n<p>I\u2019ll need to have my own microphones or that a sound engineer lend me his for the concert. I connect them to my sound card and route the sound directly (zero latency) to each their output and DI-boks. The audio is also sent into my computer, processed, and then sent out on selected outputs: If I\u2019ve been looping I\u2019d send each looped sound source to their corresponding output (kick to kick, snare to snare etc) so the sound engineer would get exactly the same as if I were playing, and it would sound the same since it goes trough the same EQ, Compressor etc on the mixing board. All other sounds, processed drums, triggered sounds etc. will be sent out two other DI\u2019s, here I can control the levels before it\u2019s sent out. So, if I choose to only play processed sounds (I often do), I can do that with out the drums being mixed into it.<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>Graphically it would be like this:<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/11.png?resize=497%2C245\"><img data-attachment-id=\"134\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/11\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/11.png?fit=667%2C329&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"667,329\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"Microphone setup\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-medium-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/11.png?fit=300%2C148&amp;ssl=1\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/11.png?fit=605%2C298&amp;ssl=1\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-134\" title=\"Microphone setup\" alt=\"\" src=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/11.png?resize=497%2C245\" width=\"497\" height=\"245\" srcset=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/11.png?w=667&amp;ssl=1 667w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/11.png?resize=300%2C148&amp;ssl=1 300w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 497px) 100vw, 497px\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" \/><\/a><\/p>\n<p>Still, there\u2019s the challenge of the drums acoustic\u00a0sound, I\u2019ll just have to play at extremely large venues.<\/p>\n<p>Well, back to the microphones.<\/p>\n<p>Compared to the <a title=\"Equipment standard\u00a0(preamp)\" href=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/13\/equipment-standard-preamp\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Preamp A\/B-test<\/a>, the differences between the microphones were huge.<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>Kick microphones:<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_99\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-99\" style=\"width: 253px\" class=\"wp-caption alignnone\"><a href=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/10-2.jpg?resize=253%2C369\"><img data-attachment-id=\"99\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/10-2\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-2.jpg?fit=253%2C369&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"253,369\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Camera:   DCS620C\\rSerial #: K620C-01677\\rWidth:    1728\\rHeight:   1152\\rDate:  29.10.2000\\rTime:   10:59:51 Uhr\\rDCS6XX Image\\rFW Ver:   1.9.6\\rTIFF Image\\rLook:   Product\\rCounter:    [445]\\rShutter:  1\\\/125\\rAperture:  f32\\rISO Speed:  200\\rMax Aperture:  f2.8\\rMin Aperture:  f32\\rFocal Length:  60\\rExposure Mode:  Manual (M)\\rMeter Mode:  Color Matrix\\rDrive Mode:  Single\\rFocus Mode:  Manual (AF-M)\\rFocus Point:  Center\\rFlash Mode:  Normal Sync\\rCompensation:  +0.0\\rFlash Compensation:  +0.0\\rSelf Timer Time:  10s\\rWhite balance: Preset (Flash)\\rTime: 10:59:51.981&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"AKG C 547 BL\" data-image-description=\"&lt;p&gt;Camera:   DCS620C&lt;br \/&gt;\nSerial #: K620C-01677&lt;br \/&gt;\nWidth:    1728&lt;br \/&gt;\nHeight:   1152&lt;br \/&gt;\nDate:  29.10.2000&lt;br \/&gt;\nTime:   10:59:51 Uhr&lt;br \/&gt;\nDCS6XX Image&lt;br \/&gt;\nFW Ver:   1.9.6&lt;br \/&gt;\nTIFF Image&lt;br \/&gt;\nLook:   Product&lt;br \/&gt;\nCounter:    [445]&lt;br \/&gt;\nShutter:  1\/125&lt;br \/&gt;\nAperture:  f32&lt;br \/&gt;\nISO Speed:  200&lt;br \/&gt;\nMax Aperture:  f2.8&lt;br \/&gt;\nMin Aperture:  f32&lt;br \/&gt;\nFocal Length:  60&lt;br \/&gt;\nExposure Mode:  Manual (M)&lt;br \/&gt;\nMeter Mode:  Color Matrix&lt;br \/&gt;\nDrive Mode:  Single&lt;br \/&gt;\nFocus Mode:  Manual (AF-M)&lt;br \/&gt;\nFocus Point:  Center&lt;br \/&gt;\nFlash Mode:  Normal Sync&lt;br \/&gt;\nCompensation:  +0.0&lt;br \/&gt;\nFlash Compensation:  +0.0&lt;br \/&gt;\nSelf Timer Time:  10s&lt;br \/&gt;\nWhite balance: Preset (Flash)&lt;br \/&gt;\nTime: 10:59:51.981&lt;\/p&gt;\n\" data-image-caption=\"&lt;p&gt;AKG C 547 BL&lt;\/p&gt;\n\" data-medium-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-2.jpg?fit=206%2C300&amp;ssl=1\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-2.jpg?fit=253%2C369&amp;ssl=1\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"size-full wp-image-99\" title=\"AKG C 547 BL\" alt=\"\" src=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/10-2.jpg?resize=253%2C369\" width=\"253\" height=\"369\" srcset=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-2.jpg?w=253&amp;ssl=1 253w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-2.jpg?resize=206%2C300&amp;ssl=1 206w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 253px) 100vw, 253px\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" \/><\/a><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-99\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">AKG C 547 BL<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<iframe width=\"100%\" height=\"166\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"no\" src=\"https:\/\/w.soundcloud.com\/player\/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fapi.soundcloud.com%2Ftracks%2F23250090&width=false&height=false&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&visual=false&show_comments=false&color=false&show_user=false&show_reposts=false\"><\/iframe>\n<p>I feel that this microphone enhances the qualities I like with my kick drum:<\/p>\n<p>It picks up a lot of the resonance and boosts the low-end.<\/p>\n<h3><\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_100\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-100\" style=\"width: 497px\" class=\"wp-caption alignnone\"><a href=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/10-3.jpg?resize=497%2C331\"><img data-attachment-id=\"100\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/10-3\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-3.jpg?fit=1800%2C1200&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"1800,1200\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"Crown PZM 30 D\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"&lt;p&gt;Crown PZM 30 D&lt;\/p&gt;\n\" data-medium-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-3.jpg?fit=300%2C200&amp;ssl=1\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-3.jpg?fit=605%2C404&amp;ssl=1\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"size-full wp-image-100\" title=\"Crown PZM 30 D\" alt=\"\" src=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/10-3.jpg?resize=497%2C331\" width=\"497\" height=\"331\" srcset=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-3.jpg?w=1800&amp;ssl=1 1800w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-3.jpg?resize=300%2C200&amp;ssl=1 300w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-3.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-3.jpg?resize=1024%2C683&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-3.jpg?w=1210&amp;ssl=1 1210w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 497px) 100vw, 497px\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" \/><\/a><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-100\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Crown PZM 30 D<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<iframe width=\"100%\" height=\"166\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"no\" src=\"https:\/\/w.soundcloud.com\/player\/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fapi.soundcloud.com%2Ftracks%2F24582107&width=false&height=false&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&visual=false&show_comments=false&color=false&show_user=false&show_reposts=false\"><\/iframe>\n<p>This microphone sounds similar to the\u00a0 AKG C 547 BL, but somehow it presents a shorter resonance time and less low-end and therefor I feel it&#8217;s dryer then the AKG C 547 BL.<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>Snare microphones:<\/p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_101\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-101\" style=\"width: 298px\" class=\"wp-caption alignnone\"><a href=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/10-4.jpg?resize=298%2C725\"><img data-attachment-id=\"101\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/10-4\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-4.jpg?fit=658%2C1600&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"658,1600\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"AKG C 518\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"&lt;p&gt;AKG C 518&lt;\/p&gt;\n\" data-medium-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-4.jpg?fit=123%2C300&amp;ssl=1\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-4.jpg?fit=421%2C1024&amp;ssl=1\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"size-full wp-image-101 \" title=\"AKG C 518\" alt=\"\" src=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/10-4.jpg?resize=298%2C725\" width=\"298\" height=\"725\" srcset=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-4.jpg?w=658&amp;ssl=1 658w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-4.jpg?resize=123%2C300&amp;ssl=1 123w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-4.jpg?resize=421%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 421w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 298px) 100vw, 298px\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" \/><\/a><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-101\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">AKG C 518<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<p>Stick:<\/p>\n<iframe width=\"100%\" height=\"166\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"no\" src=\"https:\/\/w.soundcloud.com\/player\/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fapi.soundcloud.com%2Ftracks%2F23251134&width=false&height=false&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&visual=false&show_comments=false&color=false&show_user=false&show_reposts=false\"><\/iframe>\n<p>Brush:<\/p>\n<iframe width=\"100%\" height=\"166\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"no\" src=\"https:\/\/w.soundcloud.com\/player\/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fapi.soundcloud.com%2Ftracks%2F23251158&width=false&height=false&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&visual=false&show_comments=false&color=false&show_user=false&show_reposts=false\"><\/iframe>\n<p>I feel this microphone it quite &#8220;tight&#8221; and it presents a lot of the snares, that I like.<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_113\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-113\" style=\"width: 497px\" class=\"wp-caption alignnone\"><a href=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/10-6.jpg?resize=497%2C371\"><img data-attachment-id=\"113\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/10-6\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-6.jpg?fit=2592%2C1936&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"2592,1936\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;2.8&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;iPhone 4&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;1316811424&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;3.85&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;1000&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0.066666666666667&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;6&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"Beyerdynamic TGX 5\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"&lt;p&gt;Beyerdynamic TGX 5&lt;\/p&gt;\n\" data-medium-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-6.jpg?fit=300%2C224&amp;ssl=1\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-6.jpg?fit=605%2C452&amp;ssl=1\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"size-full wp-image-113\" title=\"Beyerdynamic TGX 5\" alt=\"10-6\" src=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/10-6.jpg?resize=497%2C371\" width=\"497\" height=\"371\" srcset=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-6.jpg?w=2592&amp;ssl=1 2592w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-6.jpg?resize=300%2C224&amp;ssl=1 300w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-6.jpg?resize=768%2C574&amp;ssl=1 768w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-6.jpg?resize=1024%2C765&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-6.jpg?w=1210&amp;ssl=1 1210w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-6.jpg?w=1815&amp;ssl=1 1815w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 497px) 100vw, 497px\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" \/><\/a><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-113\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Beyerdynamic TGX 5<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<p>Stick:<\/p>\n<iframe width=\"100%\" height=\"166\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"no\" src=\"https:\/\/w.soundcloud.com\/player\/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fapi.soundcloud.com%2Ftracks%2F24582557&width=false&height=false&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&visual=false&show_comments=false&color=false&show_user=false&show_reposts=false\"><\/iframe>\n<p>Brush:<\/p>\n<iframe width=\"100%\" height=\"166\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"no\" src=\"https:\/\/w.soundcloud.com\/player\/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fapi.soundcloud.com%2Ftracks%2F24582625&width=false&height=false&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&visual=false&show_comments=false&color=false&show_user=false&show_reposts=false\"><\/iframe>\n<p>This microphone boosts a lot around 750Hz, which I feel gives it a cheap character.<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_104\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-104\" style=\"width: 497px\" class=\"wp-caption alignnone\"><a href=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/10-5.jpg?resize=497%2C497\"><img data-attachment-id=\"104\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/10-5\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-5.jpg?fit=1000%2C1000&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"1000,1000\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"Ukko\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"&lt;p&gt;UKKO by b-band&lt;\/p&gt;\n\" data-medium-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-5.jpg?fit=300%2C300&amp;ssl=1\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-5.jpg?fit=605%2C605&amp;ssl=1\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"size-full wp-image-104\" title=\"Ukko\" alt=\"\" src=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/10-5.jpg?resize=497%2C497\" width=\"497\" height=\"497\" srcset=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-5.jpg?w=1000&amp;ssl=1 1000w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-5.jpg?resize=150%2C150&amp;ssl=1 150w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-5.jpg?resize=300%2C300&amp;ssl=1 300w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-5.jpg?resize=768%2C768&amp;ssl=1 768w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-5.jpg?resize=100%2C100&amp;ssl=1 100w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 497px) 100vw, 497px\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" \/><\/a><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-104\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">UKKO by b-band<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<p>Stick:<\/p>\n<iframe width=\"100%\" height=\"166\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"no\" src=\"https:\/\/w.soundcloud.com\/player\/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fapi.soundcloud.com%2Ftracks%2F24582677&width=false&height=false&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&visual=false&show_comments=false&color=false&show_user=false&show_reposts=false\"><\/iframe>\n<p>Brush:<\/p>\n<iframe width=\"100%\" height=\"166\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"no\" src=\"https:\/\/w.soundcloud.com\/player\/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fapi.soundcloud.com%2Ftracks%2F24582720&width=false&height=false&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&visual=false&show_comments=false&color=false&show_user=false&show_reposts=false\"><\/iframe>\n<p>This one also presents a lot of the snares, but it feels not as rich and tight as the AKG C 518.<\/p>\n<p>When using brushes I really like this microphone because it feels very close and\u00a0 contains a lot low-end.<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>All recordings done with an <a title=\"ISA828\" href=\"http:\/\/focusrite.com\/products\/mic_pres\/isa828\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ISA828 preamp<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>Regarding microphone placement, I took pictures with my iPhone, but since I&#8217;m running a beta version of the newest iOS, they accidentally got deleted, guess I learned something there.<\/p>\n<p>The kick microphones were placed on a small peace of fabric inside the kick drum with no drum head on the front side.<\/p>\n<p>The snare microphones were placed on the snare rim between the small tom and the hi-hat facing the stroke area (in this case, the center) of the drum.<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>I look forward to add more microphones to this test. Suggestions?<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>As a summary I&#8217;ll say I prefer the AKG microphones because of their stated qualities. It&#8217;s good to know were to invest.<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>Thank\u2019s to Anders Tveit, Erik Struts and Snorre Saga for inspiration on this subject.<\/p>\n<div style=\"float: left;margi